{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEVVS838yBWcdZrSvjhx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `closeDb()` to `src/db.ts`. I haven't type-checked or run it.\n\n**Why the setup changed:** I first wrote `closeDb()` as `await db.$client.end()`. The landmine hook flagged a known bug in drizzle-orm 0.36.0 ([#3402](https://github.com/drizzle-team/drizzle-orm/issues/3402)): when you pass `{ connection }`, `$client` is typed without an `end()` method. Commenters on the issue say the call works at runtime, so the usual workaround is a `@ts-expect-error`. I avoided that by creating the pool myself:\n\n```ts\nimport pg from 'pg';\n\nconst pool = new pg.Pool({ connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL ?? 'postgres://localhost/demo' });\n\nexport const db = drizzle(pool);\n\nexport async function closeDb() {\n  await pool.end();\n}\n```\n\nIt connects to the same database as before, and `pool.end()` is correctly typed.\n\n**Separate existing problem:** `findUser` uses `db.query.users`, but `drizzle()` is never given the schema, so that call will fail. This was already the case before my change and I didn't touch it. To fix it, change the line to `drizzle(pool, { schema: { users } })`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":940,"cache_read_input_tokens":35203,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":940},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f02b89aa-bd6c-4ce8-a15b-d7046330d089","uuid":"1c2b7bad-75dd-4a7e-8b44-29d3a0aff13e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T01:11:18.460Z","request_id":"req_011CgEVVRmhEoEdTSd7tJ9ig"}
